  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nicoverbruggen/libron/tarball/v0.31",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nicoverbruggen/libron/zipball/v0.31",
  "body": "Hello everyone,\r\n\r\nAnother minor update today with some small improvements for European languages. If you read mostly in English, you probably don't need to install this update. Conversely, you're a German or Polish reader, you'll probably want to get this one.\r\n\r\n### Downloads\r\n\r\n- **If you are using a Kobo device**, download [KF_Libron.zip](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/releases/download/v0.31/KF_Libron.zip). It has been processed with `kobo-font-fix` for improved compatibility with Kobo's `kepub` renderer.\r\n- **If you are using KOReader**, download [Libron_R.zip](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/releases/download/v0.31/Libron_R.zip). The family appears as `Libron R` and uses 35% extra line spacing.\r\n- **If you are using CrossPoint Reader**, download [Libron_CrossPoint.zip](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/releases/download/v0.31/Libron_CrossPoint.zip). Copy the `Libron` folder into the `fonts` folder on the SD card. Each `cpfont` file includes all four styles at one reading size.\r\n- **If you are using a Kindle, another e-reader or a desktop computer**, download [Libron.zip](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/releases/download/v0.31/Libron.zip).\r\n- **If you want to use Libron on a website**, download [Libron_Web.zip](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/releases/download/v0.31/Libron_Web.zip).\r\n\r\nAn interim version of [Libron International](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32980105/Libron.International.zip) with support for more alphabets (Cyrillic and Greek, notably) is also available. (Still the same version as last time.)\r\n\r\n### Superscripts, subscripts and fractions\r\n\r\nCompleted superscript and subscript digits and added their signs and parentheses in all four styles. Adjusted the new small figures for weight, height and spacing, including italic subscript placement. Added the remaining encoded fractions.\r\n\r\nCompleted `sups` and added `subs`, `sinf`, `numr`, `dnom` and `frac`. The `frac` feature supports multi-digit fractions with `/` or `⁄` and works with proportional and tabular figures.\r\n\r\n### Unicode spaces\r\n\r\nAdded 14 Unicode spaces, including en, em, figure, punctuation, thin, hair and narrow no-break spaces.\r\n\r\n### Polish typography\r\n\r\nMoved the Polish acute accents on `ć ń ó ś ź` 50 units right in Regular and Bold.\r\n\r\n### Adjusted outlines\r\n\r\n| Weight | Glyphs |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Regular | `ó ć ı ń ś ź ǩ ȟ ḃ ḋ ḟ ḣ ḧ ḱ Ḳ Ḵ Ṃ Ṇ Ṉ Ṛ Ṟ ṫ Ṿ Ẉ ẗ ẞ` |\r\n| Bold | `ó ć ı ń ś ź ǩ ȟ ḃ ḋ ḟ ḣ ḧ ḱ Ṃ Ṇ Ṉ Ṛ Ṟ ṫ Ṿ Ẉ ẗ ẞ` |\r\n| Italic | `ḋ Ṃ Ṇ Ṉ Ṛ Ṟ ṫ Ṿ Ẉ ẗ ẞ` |\r\n| Bold Italic | `ḋ Ṃ Ṇ Ṉ Ṛ Ṟ ṫ Ṿ Ẉ ẗ ẞ` |\r\n\r\n### Updated spacing\r\n\r\n| Weight | Glyphs |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Regular | `ì í î ï ĩ ī ĭ į ı ǐ ǩ ȉ ȋ ḃ ḋ ḯ ḱ Ṇ Ṉ ṫ ẗ ẞ ỉ` |\r\n| Bold | `ṫ ẗ ẞ` |\r\n| Italic | `ẞ` |\r\n| Bold Italic | `ẞ` |\r\n\r\n### Learn more\r\n\r\nLibron is a modified version of Readerly with a calmer, more neutral appearance intended for reading books. For more information about the font and how it was built, please consult the [README](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/blob/main/README.md).\r\n\r\n### License\r\n\r\nLibron is available under the [SIL Open Font License](https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/libron/blob/main/LICENSE) and may be embedded in digital books.",
